const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is being built in Walton-on-Thames?',
    a: `Walton's recent major applications have centred on the town centre and New Zealand Avenue rather than on greenfield sites, including the former Homebase site and several High Street buildings. This page lists the major applications and their stage, as recorded on ${checkedOn}.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I comment on a planning application in Walton?',
    a: 'Search for it on Elmbridge Borough Council’s planning pages and use the comment option on the application itself. Comments have to raise material planning considerations, and the council is not required to consider anything submitted after the consultation window closes.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why are there so few large applications in Walton?',
    a: 'Walton is largely built up, so major schemes tend to be redevelopment of existing sites rather than new land, and they arrive in ones and twos. This page covers major applications only. Householder work such as extensions is far more common but is not listed here.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which council handles planning in Walton-on-Thames?',
    a: 'Elmbridge Borough Council, until 31 March 2027. From 1 April 2027 it is replaced by East Surrey Council, a unitary authority formed from Elmbridge, Epsom and Ewell, Mole Valley, Reigate and Banstead, and Tandridge.',
